# The name Pi gives, in <team home>/.pi/agent/auth.json, to the sign-in each provider of jht.config.json can run on Pi.
# Read by shared/runtime/agent-harness.js (the wizard, `jht providers harness`) and shared/skills/pi_login.py (the launcher, the status
# of the sign-in): a login of Pi counts for the provider of the setup only when its own entry is in the file.
#
# THE NAMES ARE THOSE OF Pi 1.5.0 (PI_NAMES_FROM below), read in its code and not in its docs: `/login` saves under the id of the provider
# that was chosen. They are the ids the agents start with (`--provider openai|zai|moonshotai`), so a file that passes this check is one the
# agents can use. At every update of Pi (JHT_PI_VERSION in .launcher/spawn-lib.sh) read them again: tests/test_pi_login.py fails until
# the line below names the new version.
# PI_NAMES_FROM=1.5.0
#
#   provider|Pi's names, comma separated (ChatGPT sign-in and an OpenAI API key are both `openai` in 1.5.0)
openai|openai
codex|openai
glm|zai
kimi|moonshotai
moonshot|moonshotai
